---
description: Server Actions, form state and optimistic updates
globs: app/actions/*.ts,components/auth/*.tsx,components/todos/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

## Two action shapes
**Form actions** — `(previous: ActionState, formData: FormData) => ActionState`,
driven by `useActionState`. Used by `login`, `signup`, `addTodo`.

**Direct mutations** — return `MutationResult` (`{ ok: true } | { ok: false; message }`).
Used by `setTodoCompleted`, `renameTodo`, `removeTodo`, `clearCompleted`.
They **return** failures rather than throwing: an exception escaping a Server
Action called inside a transition takes the whole route down, and one failed
toggle must never do that.

Every action starts with `await requireUser()` and ends with
`revalidatePath("/todos")`. `redirect()` throws to unwind, so it goes **outside**
the try/catch.

## ActionState
```ts
{ ok?, message?, fieldErrors?: Record<string,string[]>, values?: Record<string,string> }
```
`fieldErrors` keys match form field names so `Field` renders them inline.
`message` is the form-level banner — prefer `error.formErrors[0] ?? error.message`.

**Always echo `values` back on every failure path** (never passwords). React
resets a form once its action settles — including on failure — so without the
echo a failed login wipes what the user typed.

## Forms
Validate with the `lib/validation.ts` schema via `safeParse`, returning
`fieldErrors(parsed.error)` on failure; the API re-validates and its `details[]`
surface the same way. Wire up as `Field` + `Input`/`PasswordInput` + `Button`
with `loading={pending}`, and `FormBanner` for `state.message`.

A form whose input the user may keep typing into after submit should be
**controlled** (see the todo composer) — React's post-action reset would discard
an uncontrolled value. Restore failed values during render, guarded so anything
typed since is never clobbered; don't use an effect.

## Optimistic updates
`useOptimistic(todos, reduce)` with a discriminated-union action and a pure
reducer. Optimistic rows carry a client-minted `optimistic-` id which **must
never be sent to the API** — it only accepts UUIDs, so `isPending()` holds a
row's controls and shows a spinner until the server confirms it. Optimistic state
only survives inside a transition; form actions already run in one, manual calls
need `startTransition`. On `{ ok: false }` show `message` — the optimistic change
reverts on its own.
